PRETABLE_fmt.out -- written BEFORE the dry run of gate 1's fmtattr block (dryrun_fmt.sh), so this file's mtime proves the order.
The table is a test-variant table over the GATE BLOCK (kit_fmt.BLOCK, staged/regress/gate_build.sh), not over the product: the
probe's own two type-compatible mutants were measured by fmtbb_kill.sh (codescan/fmtfix/bb_kill.out) and are re-run here as legs.
Baseline: `git archive HEAD` (79df4277) + the 47 staged src files (staged/MD5SUMS), built in a WSL /tmp scratch clone that
carries a clone-local .MUTANT sentinel; no project tree is written.  The HEAD legs READ /tmp/gxsec-build and build/ (both hold
HEAD's sources: TREES_fmt.txt) and write nothing there.

SIBLING PARITY: N/A -- the block adds no arm to an existing dispatch; the four controls are siblings of each other and each is
  rowed by name (C3-C6), one per function, so an asymmetry would show as a missing row.
CLAIM -> ROW (each added comment sentence asserting an observable consequence):
  "drop GX_PRINTF from a declaration ... every mismatch goes silent"           -> C4 under A1, C2..C6 under A2
  "four controls, four warnings, no others"                                     -> C2 (the total), C3..C6 (one per line)
  "bootblock.c's SGI loading line must print disk offset 0x100000000"           -> R3 under M1, M2, M0 and the HEAD legs
  "where it printed the low 32 bits before the fix"                             -> R3 on the HEAD legs (offset 0x0)
  "PRIx64 -> PRIu64, or (uint64_t)(uint32_t)x ... no compiler sees it"          -> M1/M2: build warnings 0 AND R3 red
  "build_tree() above already fails this gate on any warning"                   -> M0 (HEAD's bootblock.c): its build warns
  "the rest of that class is disclosed ... not claimed"                         -> no row (a contract sentence)
GUARD FIELD vs BODY FIELD: N/A -- the block is a detector, not a guarded product path; it reads no device state.
CHANNEL, per check (the leg that must red it, and the observable that differs):
  C1 control file compiled     S3 (no misc.h)             the compiler's exit status
  C2 warnings of every kind    A1 A2 A3 S3 HEAD           the count of `warning:' lines in fmtctl.log
  C3 debug (line 6)            A2 HEAD                    a -Wformat warning on line 6
  C4 fatal (line 7)            A1 A2 HEAD                 a -Wformat warning on line 7
  C5 debugmsg (line 8)         A2 A3 HEAD                 a -Wformat warning on line 8
  C6 debugmsg_cpu (line 9)     A2 HEAD                    a -Wformat warning on line 9
  P1 rows run                  S1 (a fourth row)          the denominator of FMTBB_RESULT
  P2 rows correct              HEAD M1 M2 M0 N1 N2 N3 S1  the numerator of FMTBB_RESULT
  P3 result line               HEAD M1 M2 M0 N1 N2 N3 S1  the exact line FMTBB_RESULT=3/3
  P4 control                   N1 N2 N3                   FMTBB_CONTROL (the session ended AND bootblock.c parsed the image)
  P5 sentinel last             S2 (no FMTBB_DONE)         the log's last line
  R1 row: session ended        N2 (no binary)             the session's end
  R2 row: voldir parsed        N1 N2 N3                   bootblock.c's voldir line
  R3 row: loading offset       HEAD M1 M2 M0 N1 N2 N3     the loading line's offset text
LEGS AND THE PREDICTED RED SET (every check must red on at least one leg; base reds none):
  base        none
  head_wsl    C2 C3 C4 C5 C6 P2 P3 R3        /tmp/gxsec-build: HEAD's misc.h (no attributes) and HEAD's binary (offset 0x0)
  head_pmax   C2 C3 C4 C5 C6 P2 P3 R3        build/: the same, est's copy
  M1_radix    P2 P3 R3                       bb_mutants/M1_radix.c (PRIx64 -> PRIu64): prints 0x4294967296; build warnings 0
  M2_narrow   P2 P3 R3                       bb_mutants/M2_narrow.c ((uint64_t)(uint32_t)): prints 0x0; build warnings 0
  M0_revert   P2 P3 R3                       HEAD's bootblock.c in the fixed tree: prints 0x0; its build warns twice (:435, :442)
  A1_nofatal  C2 C4                          misc.h with GX_PRINTF dropped from fatal()'s declaration
  A2_empty    C2 C3 C4 C5 C6                 misc.h with GX_PRINTF defined empty under __GNUC__
  A3_noargs   C2 C5                          misc.h with debugmsg()'s GX_PRINTF(4, 5) -> GX_PRINTF(4, 0) (arguments unchecked)
  N1_true     P2 P3 P4 R2 R3                 the binary is /bin/true
  N2_absent   P2 P3 P4 R1 R2 R3              no binary
  N3_false    P2 P3 P4 R2 R3                 the binary is /bin/false
  S1_extrarow P1 P2 P3                       a stand-in probe printing a fourth ok row and FMTBB_RESULT=4/4
  S2_nodone   P5                             a stand-in probe printing every line but FMTBB_DONE, then one more line
  S3_noheader C1 C2 C3 C4 C5 C6              the include directory without misc.h
